Subject: SUMMARY: Installing V5.1 on DEC 3000 with no CD-ROM
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622908


Thanks to:

- Ryan McConigley <ryan@cs.uwa.edu.au>
- Hahling, Werner <hahlingw@nqn.newsltd.com.au>
- Graham Pointon <Graham.Pointon@unilever.com>
- Dr. Thomas.Blinn <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>

for their amazingly quick replies.


Consensus is: try to find an external SCSI CD-ROM drive.


Dr. Blinn pointed out that it's not worth the trouble to upgrade
since the 3000/300 is very slow (but still faster than
my DEC 5000/25 :-).

Moreover, V5.1 does not officially support the 3000 series, so
there is a chance it won't work at all.


Seems I'd better stay in 4.0F.


Thanks again !

Christian.


