Subject: Summary: Linking Networker's directories
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622867

Thanks again for all the replies, specifically

Joe.Carrico, Blair Phillips, Warren Sturm, Richard Hummers, William H.
Magill and anyone else I may have missed.  Lots of replies!

Anyways, I just did it the simplest way.

I already had a drive available with more than enough space, so I shutdown
networker, copied the nsr directory then renamed the old nsr directory to
nsr.old.  Then linked using ln -s /d1/nsr nsr and started networker backup
Easier than I though.  Thanks again all.



