> inexpensive if possible.

Thanks to the following respondants:

Alan Davis
Cathy Chandra
Charles Ballowe
Chris Bryant
Dave Love
Matthias Dolder
Richard Westlake
Selden E Ball Jr
System Administration Account
Tom Linden
Werner Rost

The consensus is that Compaq (DEC) used to have an Ada compiler but that
it is now unsupported (on Tru64). Apparently it last appeared on the
December 2000 release of the software library. Support was officially
dropped in March 2000. Several URLs were suggested for places to look for
alternatives:

http://www.adaic.org/free/
http://www.rational.com/
http://www.gnat.com/
http://www.adapower.com/links.html
http://www.adahome.com/Resources/Compilers/Free.html

Several people suggested GNAT.

Peter

