Hi Admins,

 

We're getting the following message when using the MGET command in ftp from
VMS to Tru64 (V.5.1 PK3) 

 

This example was FTPing using Tru64 to get from VMS. Parameters were ASCII,
CASE, PROMPT and NMAP $1.$2;$3 $1.$2:

 

local: wpsrefnd.pv1b remote: WPSREFND.PV1B;4

200 PORT command successful.

425-Can't build data connection for XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX

425 insufficient dynamic memory

local: z-events.pv remote: Z-EVENTS.PV;4

200 PORT command successful.

425-Can't build data connection for XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX

425 insufficient dynamic memory

 

It only seems to occur when large numbers (450 in this example) of small
programs are transferred. 

Is there any setting change we could make (at either end) to resolve this
issue?.

 

The error is intermittent

 

ES40 2 node cluster with 1Gb RAM

(sys_check has no suggestions regarding tuning)

 

$ > ulimit -a

time(seconds)        unlimited

file(blocks)         unlimited

data(kbytes)         131072

stack(kbytes)        8192

memory(kbytes)       1005680

coredump(blocks)     unlimited

nofiles(descriptors) 4096

vmemory(kbytes)      4194304

 

Swap is EAGER

$ > swapon -s

Swap partition /dev/disk/dsk13c (default swap):

    Allocated space:      1110845 pages (8.48GB)

    In-use space:           43467 pages (  3%)

    Free space:           1067378 pages ( 96%)

 

 

Total swap allocation:

    Allocated space:      1110845 pages (8.48GB)

    Reserved space:        122855 pages ( 11%)

    In-use space:           43467 pages (  3%)

    Available space:       987990 pages ( 88%)

 

Kind regards 

Lawrie Smith 
Tru64 UNIX Systems Manager
Capita Technical Services 
West Malling 

email:  lawrie.smith@capita.co.uk 
