10.0pt;font-family:Arial'>Thank you all for your reply's. Some suggested
using Samba or a product called </span></font><font face="Courier New"><span
style='font-family:"Courier New"'>NIPRINT.</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:"Courier New"'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:"Courier New"'>Definitive replyies form </span></font><font
  face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>William</span></font><font
 face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'> </span></font><font
  face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>H.</span></font><font
 face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'> </span></font><font
  face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>Magill</span></font><font
face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'> and </span></font><font
  face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>Rob</span></font><font
 face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'> </span></font><font
  face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'>Hamilton</span></font><font
face="Courier New"><span style='font-family:"Courier New"'> below:</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>Yes, Tru64 UNIX lpd is
RFC1179 compliant.&nbsp; See our web site </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>at <a
href="http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/printing/bsd.html">http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/printing/bsd.html</a>
.</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>Our lpd is routinely used in
conjunction with scores of other </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>RFC1179-compliant devices
and systems, including those made </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>by HP, Lexmark, Xerox, Emulex,
AXIS, Sun, SGI, WinNT/2K, etc. </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>Tru64 lpd also supports some
non-RFC1179 extensions, such as </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>specifying input-tray,
output-bin, number-up, and sides.&nbsp; </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>But those options are only
sent in the CF (&quot;lpd Control File&quot;) </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>if a user specifies
corresponding options on the lpr command </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>line (-I, -o, -K, -N).&nbsp;
Jobs that specify those options are </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>not strictly RFC1179
compliant.&nbsp; But they are not used or </span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:"Courier New"'>included in the CF by default.</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:"Courier New"'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-autospace:none'><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span
style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:"Courier New"'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><font size=2 face="Courier New"><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
font-family:"Courier New"'>Tru64 is compliant; NT is not. </span></font><font
face=Wingdings><span style='font-family:Wingdings'>J</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><font size=2 face=Arial><span lang=EN-GB style='font-size:
10.0pt;font-family:Arial'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

<p><font size=2 face=Tahoma><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

<p><font size=2 face=Tahoma><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma'>Kind
regards </span></font></p>

<p><font size=2 face=Tahoma><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma'>Lawrie</span></font><font
 size=2 face=Tahoma><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma'> </span></font><font
  size=2 face=Tahoma><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma'>Smith</span></font><font
size=2 face=Tahoma><span style='font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Tahoma'> <br>
Tru64 UNIX Systems Manager<br>
Capita Technical Services <br>
West Malling </span></font></p>

<p><font size=3 face="Times New Roman"><span style='font-size:12.0pt'>email:&nbsp;
lawrie.smith@capita.co.uk <br>
Tel:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 01732 877266 <br>
Mob:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 0774 082 5468</span></font></p>

<p class=MsoHeader><font size=2 face="Times New Roman"><span lang=EN-GB
style='font-size:10.0pt'>&nbsp;</span></font></p>

