replaced it...but the system kept crashing.&nbsp; They couldn't really =
find any
hard evidence to point at a definite piece of hardware...so we had them =
replace
ALL the CPUs with new ones, and the system has been up for
almost&nbsp;24&nbsp;hours now (previously it hasn't stayed up for more =
than a
couple of hours...and usually closer to 15 minutes.).&nbsp; They also =
had found
that one of the KGPSA cards was in an &quot;illegal =
configuration&quot;.&nbsp;
Im not sure what this means, but they said that it had to be in a =
certain slot
on the bus, so they just moved it over one slot.&nbsp; They said it =
(the card)
wasn't causing any obvious problems, but figured they would put it in =
the
correct slot anyway.&nbsp; </span></font><o:p></o:p></p>

</div>

<div>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-left:.5in'><font size=3D2 =
face=3DArial><span
style=3D'font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial'>I'm not saying that anyone =
from
compaq has any clue what exactly was (is?) wrong with this machine, but
replacing ALL the CPUs was the only thing that actually seemed to =
help.&nbsp;
We have had&nbsp;people coming in from Compaq for the past week and a =
half
trying to fix this machine, and today they finally left, and everything =
seems
to be fine.&nbsp; But honestly, I don't feel very satisfied...it could =
crash
again tonight.&nbsp; Sure we replaced all the CPUs, but they were all =
new to
begin with...so who knows if they really fixed the problem.&nbsp; =
</span></font><o:p></o:p></p>

</div>

<div>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-left:.5in'><font size=3D2 =
face=3DArial><span
style=3D'font-size:10.0pt;font-family:Arial'>I feel terrible that you =
are
starting the journey that I (hopefully) just finished...it was a =
terrible
terrible time.&nbsp; I hope my story can shed some light onto the =
problem you
are having.&nbsp; good luck...=3D/</span></font><o:p></o:p></p>

