From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Mar 20 15:29:47 2002
From: Steven Michael ROBBINS <stever () po-box-cgrl-lab ! cs ! mcgill ! ca>
Date: Wed, 20 Mar 2002 15:29:47 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: system hangs when I type "who" or "ps" or ...
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622797

Hello,

I'm running Digital UNIX V4.0F on a DECStation 3000.

The system got into a weird state last week, in which it
still serves NFS and web as normal, but if I log in and type
"who" or "ps" or some other commands, my terminal session
hangs --- neither ^C nor ^Z can get the shell back.

I rebooted a few days back but the problem returned.

Searching through the list archives, I found the summary
to a similar question

  http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/tru64-unix-managers/2000/05/msg00497.html

In the responses, someone suggested to trace the system calls
of ps, which I did.  It gets stuck on a stat() call:

    ...
    stat ("/dev/ttyp2", 0x11fffee90) =


And so I of course did "ls -l /dev/ttyp2" and promptly hung yet
another terminal session ... I can't run "lsof" to find out
the process using this tty either ...

Does this ring any bells?  Maddeningly, I had this problem 
years ago, but I can't recall how I fixed it, and I can't
find my notes!

Desperately yours,
-Steve

From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Mar 20 14:52:06 2002
From: Nick Goodman <ngoodman () AmericanExcelsior ! com>
Date: Wed, 20 Mar 2002 14:52:06 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Quick Question, performance decrease moving from 4.0d to	4.0f
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622796

Problem Solved, thanks to the few that replied but ended up being a simple
solution.

The Cron defrag routine was running at the same time as the database backups
were, we simply changed the time defragcron ran and we are back to our
normal times.

Thanks.

Previous email:

Forgive me if this sounds stupid, but I've just been thrown into
learning
Unix quicker than I expected.  Anyways, here is the setup:
Alpha 4100 with 2/533 and 2 gig RAM
4.0f with cumulative patch kit
Progress 8.3b and MFG/PRO 8.5e.

Database sits on a RAID 0+1 set, and is taken offline at 2 am everynight
for
a backup using the progress probak util.  Before the upgrade to 4.0f it
would take approximately an hour to backup to a different drive, now
after
the upgrade it takes about 2 hours, and seems to take longer everyday.
Now
here is the kicker, after moving to 4.0f we purged about 20% of our
records
in the database, and it is taking just as long.

Are there any known performance issues with 4.0f?  I appreciate any help
at
all.  Thanks!

From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Mar 20 14:45:54 2002
From: Donald_Bowers () shamrockfoods ! com
Date: Wed, 20 Mar 2002 14:45:54 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SMTP Error Code 501
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622795


RE: SMTP Error Code 501

I want to thank all of those who responded for their input.  We actually
discovered the problem by checking the logs on our Notes (mail) server.
Seems that Metrocall is set up for anti-spamming and is confirming incoming
mail by doing a reverse lookup on the incoming e-mail/hostname.  In our
case the e-mail being sent has an address that is fully qualified -
including the machine name.  Our internal machines are not known to the
outside world so the e-mail is being "bounced" by Metrocall.  We are
working on a solution to this problem - but at least we now know what the
problem is.

Again, thanks for everyone's input.

- dwb

