From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Mar 15 18:51:29 2002
From: Chris Adams <cmadams () hiwaay ! net>
Date: Fri, 15 Mar 2002 18:51:29 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: Signal handling bug in 5.1A?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622746

Once upon a time, Chris Adams <cmadams@hiwaay.net> said:
> I just upgraded (really a clean install) our primary mail server from
> 4.0F to 5.1A Friday morning.  I rebuilt all the software that we use,
> including sendmail 8.12.2 (we use some features that aren't available in
> Compaq's build of sendmail).
> 
> After a few hours, sendmail stopped accepting new connections.  I tried
> to restart it, but the master daemon process was stuck in an
> uninterruptable sleep (ps showed "U" for the state).  I couldn't start a
> new sendmail daemon because the old one still held the socket open.  So,
> we had to reboot the server.

Well, the signal handling bit was a red herring; the real problem was
that whenever sendmail tried to close the listening socket, it got stuck
(both the process and the socket).

The fix was a patch from Compaq - there is a problem with closing
sockets (I guess only busy sockets) in 5.1A.  It is a post-kit1 patch (I
forgot to say initially that I did have kit1 installed).
-- 
Chris Adams <cmadams@hiwaay.net>
Systems and Network Administrator - HiWAAY Internet Services
I don't speak for anybody but myself - that's enough trouble.

