From: "Hines, Bruce D" <bruce.hines () eds ! com>
Date: Tue, 12 Mar 2002 16:26:38 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Using EMC PowerPath with TruCluster v1.6
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622693

Thanks to:

"We run a two node cluster on TruCluster v1.6.  The powerpath software has
to go on both nodes as there is no common root disk and therefore both nodes
have to have a separate operating system."
 - Lewis Handy

"NEVER run Powerpath on a 4.x system, even on one node (and I'm not sure
it's possible).  We made the test and when a service reallocates, you've got
crash dump and corrupt of data.  This is a well known problem due to the
fact powerpath hides informations to the system."
 - Emmanuel Bove

This was EMC's answer:  We are wrong it is NOT supported in your
configuration.  Now, can we have a napkin to wipe the egg off our face.



