Hi,

The original message is below.  Thanks for all of the answers (and sorry for
the late summary).  The gist of the problem is that Trucluster in 4.0x and
TruCluster in 5.xx are different products and therefore not covered in any
right to use clauses in contracts of any sort.  We ended up having to
purchase these licenses from our reseller.  There are "migration" licenses
which are discounted licenses for people upgrading their systems from 4.0x.
Other than this (and a little issue with initial boot and HSG controllers),
the cluster seems to be running great.  

Michael Wheelock
Integris Health 




> Hi,
> 
> I am currently upgrading an ES/40 cluster (4.0F/1.6) to 5.1A.  We
purchased a new machine to become the first cluster member.  We will then
migrate one of the cluster services to the new machine and so on...  In the
end, we will still have a two node cluster and a test machine.  I purchased
base and server licenses for the new machine figuring that I would input the
TruCluster license from the first box I am migrating.  In the end, I would
still have the same license situation as before.  Unfortunately, clu_create
tells me that the TruCluster software must be licensed before I run
clu_create.  We have a software upgrade contract for these machines.  My
question is, what specific license is it looking for and how can I obtain
it?  Any info would be appreciated.  Thanks.
> 
> Michael Wheelock
> Integris Health

