Date: Mon, 04 Mar 2002 07:47:55 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Disklabel and A partition
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622545

Dear Managers

First of all. Thanks to Mike D Cross, Bryan Lavelle, Don L Rye, Pat
O'Brien, Vincent D'Antonio, Chris Ruhnke, Bruce D. Hines and Olle
Eriksson for the quick and good answers to my question.

Olle hit the spot by writing "You are trying to change the a-partition
and that is open because rz9 defaults into rz9a. Have you tried putting
an explicit rz9c in the command?"=20
And Bruce with "you can't write to an empty partition, using rz9
defaults to rz9a"

Now I understand why I get an error about the Open partition.=20

In the end I think I must do as Chris surgested: "I think your problem
is where you are trying to "zero" the "a" partition. Just leave it with
131072 blocks allocated.  There must always be space in the "a"
partition for "root" even if you do not use it for such."

Once again.=20
Thanks a lot to all of you.

Best regards and have a nice weeken
Gregers Nakman

