From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Mar 14 14:00:11 2002
From: "Eiler, James A." <James.Eiler () alcoa ! com>
Date: Thu, 14 Mar 2002 14:00:11 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Finding current number of processes
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=102653731622724

ORIGINAL QUESTION:

I'm running Tru64 5.1.

>From a C program, I need to find out how many processes are currently =
in the
system.

Is there a cfg_subsys_query( ) call I can make that will return the =
value
I'm looking for?

ANSWERS FROM:

alan@nabeth.cxo.cpqcorp.net
Oisin McGuinness
Paul A Sand
Hannes Visagie
Zelen=E1k G=E1bor

++++++

	The number of processes running or the number of processes
	allowed?  The number running isn't a configuration parameter
	and probably won't have a handle.  The other may be, but it
	could also be dynamic.

	For the number running, count the number of files in /proc.

+++++++

